<title>NEW ZEALAND: RBNZ's Brash says higher min wage inflationary.</title>
<headline>RBNZ's Brash says higher min wage inflationary.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reserve Bank of New Zealand Governor Don Brash on Tuesday said the new National-New Zealand First Party coalition government's intention to increase the adult minimum wage was likely to add to inflationary pressures.</p>
<p>In a speech, Brash said the coalition agreement envisaged a 10 percent increase in the adult minium wage on March 1, 1997, to NZ$7.00 per hour from $6.375 per hour.</p>
<p>There would also be an immediate review of the minimum wage rates for under 20s and a subsequent decision on whether or not to increase the adult minimum wage further to $7.50/hour in from March 1998.</p>
</text>
